    "22217cd1f844d8bd1c46892cb90ad95776a87170f64dfb7c2a5b06e2d91541b4": {
      "normalizationVersion": 1,
      "sourceHash": "7e5a828e1e34546b0c8d48517173a24f7534233cbd336348977baa0d7a0ae059",
      "contextFingerprint": "072b197843cae28436a378700ef3f2568bde320cf3444b92efb9b4456a19de6f",
      "sourceText": "- 对 `score_ref()`（返回 `int&`）而言，引用性就是它的全部价值所在——一旦丢了，`a` 就成了和原变量毫无关系的副本。`decltype(auto)` 的作用就是把这层引用性保住。\n- 对 `score_ptr()`（返回 `int*`）而言，它本身就不是引用，是一个**普通的值**（哪怕这个值碰巧是个地址）。`auto` 推导普通值类型时本来就不会发生\"丢引用\"的事，所以推导出来天然就是 `int*`，和 `decltype(auto)` 推导结果没有任何区别。\n**真正决定\"能不能改到原变量\"的，从来不是 `auto` 还是 `decltype(auto)`，而是你拷贝的这个值里，是否仍然携带着指向原对象的\"路径\"**：\n \n- 拷贝 `int` 值 —— 路径断了，改不到。\n- 拷贝 `int*`（地址值） —— 路径还在，*解引用*之后照样能改到。",
      "translatedText": "- For `score_ref()` (returning `int&`), referentiality is its entire value—once lost, `a` becomes a copy with no relation to the original variable\\. `decltype(auto)`'s role is to preserve this referentiality\\.\n- For `score_ptr()` (returning `int*`), it itself is not a reference but an **ordinary value** (even if this value happens to be an address)\\.`auto`When deducing an ordinary value type, \"reference loss\" never occurs in the first place, so what is deduced is naturally `int*`, with no difference whatsoever from the result deduced by `decltype(auto)`\\. **What truly determines \"whether the original variable can be modified\" is never `auto` versus `decltype(auto)`; rather, it is whether the value you copy still carries a \"path\" pointing to the original object**：\n \n- Copying the `int` value — the path is broken, so it cannot be modified\\.\n- Copying `int*` (the address value) — the path is still there, and after *dereferencing*, it can still be modified\\.",
      "provider": "deepseek",
      "model": "deepseek-flash",
      "usage": {
        "inputTokens": 302,
        "outputTokens": 209,
        "costUsd": 0.000342
      }
    },
